---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const nav = `<strong>Start</strong><a href="/docs">Overview</a><a href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart</a><strong>Build</strong><a href="/docs/api">API reference</a><a href="/docs/integrations">SDK &amp; frameworks</a><a href="/docs/multilingual" class="active">Multilingual</a><strong>Run</strong><a href="/docs/hosting">Hosting</a><a href="/docs/security">Security</a>`;
---
<Base title="Memflex multilingual — every language" desc="Language-neutral core, in-kind answers, 5-minute language plugins. Built for the whole world." path="/docs/multilingual">
<div class="wrap" style="padding:64px 24px">
  <span class="eyebrow">Docs · Multilingual</span>
  <h1>Every language. No favorites.</h1>
  <div class="docs-grid" style="margin-top:30px">
    <nav class="docs-nav" set:html={nav}></nav>
    <div class="doc">
      <h2>Guarantees</h2>
      <p>Same-language repeats work in <strong>any</strong> language (14 tested: Hindi→Arabic). The serving path has no preferred language — the LLM is instructed to answer in the user's language, regression-tested with a provider spy.</p>
      <h2>Language plugins</h2>
      <p><code>reflex/core/normalizer.py → LANGUAGE_MAPS</code>: Hindi Devanagari↔Roman convergence, German umlaut folding (<code>Rückerstattung ≡ Rueckerstattung</code>, sim 1.0 live) + intent synonyms. Scripts are never stripped; stopwords keep short queries from colliding across languages.</p>
      <h2>Add your language (5 min)</h2>
      <div class="codeblock"><button class="copy">Copy</button><pre># 1. reflex/core/normalizer.py → LANGUAGE_MAPS["french"] = &#123;...&#125;
# 2. tests/test_multilingual.py → repeat cases (must hit pure reflex)
# 3. reflex/llm/base.py → _INTENTS answers in-kind (optional)
# 4. EMBEDDING_BACKEND=hash python -m pytest tests -q  (twice)</pre></div>
      <p>Paraphrase-across-languages needs a semantic backend (<code>bge-m3</code>); the keyless <code>hash</code> backend matches repeats in every language.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</Base>
